Consider the C function foo and the binary tree shown.<br><pre><code>
typedef struct node {
   int val;
   struct node *left, *right;
} node;

int foo(node *p) {
   int retval;
   if (p == NULL)
       return 0;
else {
     retval = p->val + foo(p->left) + foo(p->right);
     printf("%d ", retval);
     return retval;
     }
}
</code></pre><br><br><img src="/wp-content/uploads/GATE/CS/20231/q37.jpg" /><br>When foo is called with a pointer to the root node of the given binary tree, what
will it print?
